Each box is chosen with probability $\frac{1}{3}$. The chance of drawing a white ball is $1$ from the all-white box, $0$ from the all-black box, and $\frac{1}{2}$ from the mixed box.

The weights are therefore $\frac{1}{3}$, $0$, and $\frac{1}{6}$, with a total of $\frac{1}{2}$ on drawing white.

P(\text{mixed} \mid \text{white}) = \frac{1/6}{1/2} = \frac{1}{3}
